    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d375">

                <pb facs="0514" n="404" sameAs="frus:frus1931v03/pg404"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/2533: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-09T16:00:00-05:00">November 9, 1931—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>411. Reference your 892, November 9, 10 a.m.; 893, November 9, 3 p.m.; 896,
                    November 9, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="78" xml:id="d375-f1"/> and Tientsin’s November 9,
                    3 p.m., to the Legation.<anchor n="79" xml:id="d375-f2"/></p>
                <list>
                    <label>(1)</label>
                    <item>Please request the Consul General at Tientsin to collaborate with Colonel
                            Taylor<anchor n="80" xml:id="d375-f3"/> and to report telegraphically
                        their conclusions regarding the cause of the fighting; who began it; if
                        American lives and property are in danger; and if, in their opinion, any
                        necessity exists for establishing the 300-metre zone outside the Japanese
                        Concession.</item>
                    <label>(2)</label>
                    <item>Inform the Consul General that he is authorized to participate if the
                        consular body at Tientsin believes it advisable to make an impartial, united
                        investigation, but he is not to take the initiative in organizing an
                        investigation of this sort.</item>
                    <label>(3)</label>
                    <item>Instruct him to report with promptness directly to the Department, as well
                        as to the Legation, concerning all matters connected with the
                        foregoing.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d375-f1" n="78" xml:id="d375-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d375-f2" n="79" xml:id="d375-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram of November 9, 4 p.m., from the Consul General at Tientsin to the
                    Department, <ref target="#pg402">p. 402</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d375-f3" n="80" xml:id="d375-f3-content">
                <p>Commanding U. S. Fifteenth Infantry Regiment, Tientsin.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
